package components

// PCORateLimitBanner is the actual "Planning Center's rate limit was
// reached" notice markup (see
// docs/plans/shipped/pco-rate-limit-user-visibility-plan.md) - pulled out
// of internal/views/layout.templ into this dependency-free leaf package
// so both internal/views (Layout's own full-page banner) and
// internal/views/scheduling (SyncCheck's fragment-level OOB banner,
// sets_publish.go/set_builder.templ) can render the exact same markup
// without an import cycle - internal/views and internal/views/scheduling
// can't import each other (see CLAUDE.md's Architecture section on why
// cross-package templ components live here instead).
//
// Deliberately calmer than an alert or invitation-style banner: not
// .warning-style alarm (nothing is broken, and PCO itself already
// recovers) and not .import-banner's "invitation" framing (there's no
// action to take here) - see pco-rate-limit-banner.css's own doc comment
// for the token choice that keeps it reading as a quiet heads-up rather
// than either of those.
templ PCORateLimitBanner() {
	<div class="pco-ratelimit-banner" role="status">
		<p>Planning Center's rate limit was reached - some details may be stale and will refresh shortly.</p>
	</div>
}
